# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. Never commit imagery or annotations.
#
# data_raw/ additionally holds a restricted clinical package that is licensed
# "collaborator research copy, no public license granted" with pixel-level PHI
# review still pending. It must not reach any remote under any circumstance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bare names as well as trailing-slash forms: these paths may be directories on
# one machine and symlinks to external storage on another, and a pattern ending
# in "/" matches only directories, so the symlink would otherwise be untracked
# and offered up for commit.
data_raw
data_raw/
data_clean/
data_clean_cp/
data_coco/
data_external/
data/
# Anything else that materialises the corpus. The copy-paste set was missed by
# the explicit list above and reached the remote as a result, so match by prefix
# rather than by enumeration.
data_*/

# ...except the anonymised COCO annotations. No imagery, no identifiers,
# and they are what makes the reported numbers reproducible. This has to sit
# after `data_*/` above, since git honours the last matching rule, and a file
# cannot be re-included while its parent directory is still excluded.
!data_coco/
data_coco/*
!data_coco/annotations/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Split file lists are regenerated deterministically by
# tools/make_clean_split.py (seed 42), so nothing is lost by ignoring them --
# and the source filenames embed patient names, which must not be republished.
splits/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weights and run artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
weights/
runs/
preds/
logs/
reports/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal: working notes, protocol drafts, machine-specific
# launchers. Kept out of the published repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_internal/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials -- belt and braces; these live in $HOME, not here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kaggle.json
access_token
.env
*.key
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Plain-language internal overview -- not part of the published repo
PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md

# Runtime pause switch for watchdog.sh -- machine state, not source
PAUSE
data_frac25/
data_frac50/
data_frac75/
data_clean_dn/
data_selftrain/
data_tooth/

# latex build artifacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out

# Packaged deliverable weights. The rule `weights/` above matches ANY directory
# of that name at any depth, including this one, which silently kept the
# manifest out of a commit that claimed to add it. Re-include the directory,
# then exclude only the binaries: the README and checksums are documentation and
# belong in the repo, the 1.3 GB of checkpoints do not.
!deliverable/weights/
deliverable/weights/**/*.pt
deliverable/weights/**/*.pth
